For a small segment, $ds^2=dx^2+dy^2,$ and therefore $ds=dx\sqrt{1+\left(\frac{dy}{dx}\right)^2}.$ Adding all the little segments gives the length $\mathcal S[y]
 =\int_{x_1}^{x_2}
   \sqrt{1+\left(y'(x)\right)^2}\,dx.$

